====================================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE ROTATION INTERPRETATION: beta_inner = -0.10 as angular momentum
====================================================================================================
  (a) DISPERSION reading: beta = 1 - sigma_t^2/sigma_r^2 ->
      sigma_t/sigma_r = sqrt(1 - beta) = 1.0485 +- 0.0351 (tangential per-axis dispersion +4.85% above radial; z vs 1 = +1.38)
  (b) ORDERED-ROTATION reading (coherent v_tan on an isotropic background, 
      sigma_t^2 = sigma_r^2 + v_rot^2/2 -> beta = -v_rot^2/(2 sigma_r^2)):
      v_rot/sigma_r = sqrt(-2 beta) = 0.446 +- 0.165
      at sigma_r,core = 844 km/s:  v_rot = 376 +- 139 km/s
  THE ANGULAR-MOMENTUM BUDGET (the shell's mean radius r = <R> R500 = 0.595 Mpc):
      specific j_core = r v_rot = 2.239e+05 kpc.km/s = 6.908e+27 m^2/s per unit mass
      L = N m r v_tan:  N = 10,145 (paper total) -> L = 6.359e-01 kg m^2/s;
      N = 3146 (the measured [0.2,1.5] shell) -> L = 1.972e-01 kg m^2/s
      (the SI numbers are small because m = 5.09 keV is a particle-scale mass; 
       the physically comparable numbers are the SPECIFIC j and the ratio to the infall's j)
  [PASS] C2 [part 1] the sigma_t/sigma_r and v_rot/sigma_r readings computed from the committed beta_inner
